# What this repository's release needs that another's does not. See propensive/.github, which
# holds the workflow and the script; a release is cut by `git tag -s X.Y.Z && git push --tags`.
# One `key value` line each; the library list is not declared, because release.sh derives it
# from `release.stage`, and the version is the tag's alone.
#
# crux publishes libraries and no executable, so its release is a draft until every asset's
# digest has been checked; there is no `launcher` and no `hints`. Once the release is public, the
# same artifacts go to Maven Central too (etc/publish-central.sh): crux alone is published there,
# so that a build can load it with no resolver declared.

name       crux
title      Crux

build      __.compile
after      ./etc/publish-central.sh
